{#
  Renders from content/igcse/* (docs/CONTENT_MODEL.md) instead of the legacy
  {% include "tracks/igcse.html" %} — nineteenth track cut over, following the established
  pattern (docs/DECISIONS/0005 through 0019). index.html's igcse-* sections and
  src/_includes/tracks/igcse.html are UNCHANGED and no longer read by this page, kept as the
  rollback path. build.js's MIGRATED_TRACKS set skips regenerating this file.

  Notes (WP31): igcse has 11 chapters, no "about" chapter (starts directly at ch.1, matching
  precalc/geo). Confirms the syllabusMapBlock (ADR 0018, sat) IS reused, exactly as predicted —
  found in ig-transform (ch.7), not ch.1, with the real per-row differences ADR 0018 anticipated:
  1-2 tags per row (Core/Extended tier badges) instead of sat's always-one, and NO inline style
  on the tag spans (sat's real tags carry style="font-size:11px"; igcse's don't).

  chapterTag reuses the 'category' variant but with a genuinely new deviation: MULTIPLE tier
  badges after the category name (📌 <strong>Topic N</strong> <span class="tier-c">C</span>
  <span class="tier-e">E</span> · ...) instead of a single weightBadge — added chapterTag.badges[]
  to the category variant (the same array shape 'pill' already used, not duplicated). Some
  individual topic strings ALSO carry an inline tier badge suffix (e.g. "Surds <span
  class="tier-e">E</span>") — no schema change needed, since topics[] entries are already raw
  HTML strings (this site's Nunjucks env runs with autoescape:false throughout).

  ig-transform's explorer control is a real <select> with NO valueDisplayId, and its live value
  is a bare <b id class="mono"> embedded INSIDE the note's own body text ("Mapping: <b
  id="igTransRule">...") — this is the SAME "block.note's embedded-<b> trick" explorer.njk's own
  docstring already documents from an earlier track; no new mechanism needed, just written
  correctly here.

  Found+fixed TWO real markup-corruption bugs, not reproduced: a stray literal `">` sitting right
  after a formula-card's closing </div> (ig-coordinate's "Intercepts" card, ig-trig's
  "Back-bearing" card) — genuine source typos that would otherwise render literally on the page,
  dropped during transcription (same fix-not-reproduce precedent as apab's/sat's markup bugs).
#}
